# `/press`, ANCHORED, and the leading slash is the whole point rather than style.
#
# Unanchored, `press` matches a file OR DIRECTORY named `press` at ANY depth —
# which includes `cmd/press/`, this service's own serving entry point. Measured
# on the tree that carried it: `git check-ignore -v cmd/press/main.go` answered
# `.gitignore:1:press`, `git ls-files cmd/press` was empty, and a clean checkout
# held `cmd/press-migrate/`, `cmd/press-claim/` and `cmd/press-gate/` while the
# binary that actually serves `/v1/ingest` existed only on the machine that wrote
# it. `mise run build` is `go build ./cmd/press`, so a fresh clone could not build
# the service at all — and the failure names a missing DIRECTORY, which reads as a
# tree that never had one rather than as a file an ignore rule was hiding.
#
# What it is meant to ignore is the compiled binary at the repository root, which
# is what `/press` matches and nothing else.
/press

# The `cf` CLI's local cache, committed by accident on a checkout where the
# tool had run. It holds the account id the tool resolved on THAT machine and
# nothing here reads it; every `cf` invocation rewrites it. The same failure
# mode as the other generated-file entries: one `git add -A` from coming back.
/.cloudflare/
keyring/
secrets/
